{"kind":"report","text":"READY-FOR-REVIEW at exact clean head c8bf52e814fe63a7733037bc69294c93ac02a0ca. F1 and F3 stay closed. F2 first half: the parented class gets a candidate-only line with no identity field, on the ground that parentlessness is checked before any decode precisely so retention does not depend on the intent being well-formed — so the decodable and undecodable cases produce the same line, which is what makes the class total rather than needing a second form. Aligned through the grammar block, the identity rule, both classification steps, refusal keying, the dedup and one-line-per-ref paragraphs, the parented-class bullet and its cost paragraph, the submitter's lookup, and hostile run 3, which now executes twice, decodable and undecodable, and requires the same line from both. F2 second half: option b. Retaining the listing was considered and rejected in the note, because the listing would be authored and signed by the accused drain, a push certificate is submitter-produced and proves a push rather than survival to drain time, and only a forge-signed listing would settle it. The note now says plainly that this is a drain assertion no reader, auditor or submitter can convict or acquit, withdraws the claim that producing the canonical ref is the same move as producing a parented candidate, and narrows the without-trusting-the-drain claim, both terminal-record passages, and the spike auditor assertion to match, with a sixth hostile run pinning the residue as a limit. One addition rather than a narrowing: a new mechanical check requires the recomputed canonical ref to appear on no line at that candidate, so a drain that misfiles it as noncanonical-ref is caught and only total suppression works. Merging main also falsified several measured passages, which are rewritten rather than left lying: kernel key rotation is now implemented, so the epoch paragraph and R3 are rebuilt around Rotate and the two scans, with the absence of any operator surface flagged; admission-profile governance shipped, so the measurements claiming the fold has no such machinery are replaced. One divergence is recorded rather than resolved: the shipped kind requires bundle, contract and genesis and reports the activation's contract as the version, which is the shape this note argues against. I did not flip the note; it states the disagreement and says the kind should move. That is a design judgement made in the course of this repair, and it is the reviewer's to accept or reject. Five claims I am not confident in, named rather than buried: that re-pushing the same object under its canonical ref reaches admission on a later batch, which I reasoned from dedup keying rather than a specified rule; the judged-ref rule for classes with no canonical ref, which slightly widens what noncanonical-ref means; that no mainstream forge offers a signed ref listing, stated from knowledge and not measured; the contract-field judgement above; and the rotation description, read from the kernel source without executing a rotation. Gates: make vet clean, make test all fifteen packages ok, git diff --check clean.","body":{"head":"c8bf52e814fe63a7733037bc69294c93ac02a0ca"}}